A bakery-standard chocolate chip cookie featuring a balanced ratio of white and brown sugars, aromatic vanilla, and plenty of semi-sweet chocolate chips. Crisp along the edges with a tender, chewy middle.

*Adapted from [Ghirardelli](https://www.ghirardelli.com/chocolate-chip-cookies-rec1016).*

## Ingredients

- 2 ¼ cups all-purpose flour (approx. 270g)
- 1 teaspoon baking soda
- ½ teaspoon salt
- 1 cup (2 sticks) unsalted butter, softened to room temperature
- ¾ cup granulated sugar (approx. 150g)
- ¾ cup packed light brown sugar (approx. 165g)
- 2 large eggs, room temperature
- 2 teaspoons pure vanilla extract
- 2 cups semi-sweet chocolate chips (approx. 12 oz)
- 1 cup chopped walnuts or pecans, lightly toasted (optional)

## Instructions

1. **Preheat the Oven:** Set your oven to 375°F (190°C). Position oven racks in the upper and lower thirds. Line baking sheets with parchment paper or silicone mats for effortless release and easy clean-up.
2. **Whisk the Dry Foundation:** In a medium bowl, whisk together the flour, baking soda, and salt until aerated and thoroughly distributed.
3. **Cream the Fats and Sugars:** In the bowl of an electric stand mixer fitted with the paddle (or using a handheld electric mixer), beat the softened butter, white granulated sugar, and brown sugar together on medium speed for 2 to 3 minutes until the texture becomes fluffy, pale, and thoroughly creamed.
4. **Beat in Eggs and Vanilla:** Add the room-temperature eggs one at a time, followed by the vanilla extract. Mix on low-to-medium speed until each egg is fully emulsified into the creamed butter.
5. **Combine Dry and Wet:** Lower the mixer speed and gradually pour in the flour mixture in three installments, stopping as soon as the last flour streaks disappear. Gently fold in the chocolate chips and optional toasted nuts using a wooden spoon or spatula.
6. **Drop and Bake:** Scoop rounded tablespoons of dough (about 1.5 tablespoons each) and place onto the baking sheets, leaving 2 inches between cookies to accommodate spread.
7. **Bake to Light Golden:** Bake at 375°F for 9 to 11 minutes. Watch closely: remove when edges have set and turned a warm golden color while the center looks slightly underdone and soft.
8. **Cool and Serve:** Allow the cookies to settle on the warm pans for 2 minutes, then slide a spatula underneath and transfer them to a wire rack to finish cooling.

## Notes

- **Cookie Texture Tip:** Chilling the scooped dough balls in the refrigerator for 30–60 minutes before baking prevents over-spreading and yields a thicker, chewier cookie with richer flavor development.
- **Nut Toasting:** If adding walnuts or pecans, toast them in a dry skillet over medium heat for 3 to 5 minutes until fragrant, then let cool completely before folding into the dough.
- **Storage:** Keep cooled cookies in an airtight container at room temperature with a slice of plain sandwich bread for up to 5 days; the moisture from the bread keeps the cookies wonderfully soft.
